      "id": 6162,
      "name": "Irish Bear",
      "username": "Irish_Bear",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/irish_bear/{size}/2557_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-08-15T16:31:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Well, when playing Sentinels for a while, with the same heroes, and the same villains, some folks feel a bit burned out on doing the same thing.&nbsp; And with the 2nd expansion soon in hand, we'll be able to get our energy back.&nbsp; While in the mean time, me and my friends have been developing Video game-themed decks.&nbsp; As the usual DM, I'm in the mest of creating a Villain Deck, from scratch, with it's own playstyle, that goes along with the Villain, who's based off of a popular videogame character.&nbsp; My friends are each creating their own Hero deck, from different generes, again, with their own playstyles and powers.&nbsp; I'm just about half way done with the concept and developing, all there is left is to playtest with my friends, and will soon showcase our efforts in the future.&nbsp; It's fan-made, so not trying to claim original characters, just using them as themes.&nbsp; Hopefully, it works out great, and will give folks something interesting to try if they want.&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
