      "id": 36330,
      "name": "Koga",
      "username": "Koga",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/{size}/2058_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-08-20T03:33:11.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>And if you haven't checked out my templates you probably should, especially if you have Adobe Illustrator. A great way to make the cards look official or to make them still fit in while playtesting.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/forum/topic/custom-card-templates\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/forum/topic/custom-card-templates</a></p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Cool.&nbsp; There are a bunch of fan-made heroes and villains on the SotM Boardgame Geek page too, if you're looking for something new.&nbsp; Seems like most of them get posted before playtesting rather than after, though, so your mileage may vary.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It's kind of the point to post them before or during early playtesting, to get feedback on them so they can get balanced out, I know it helped my first hero a lot, but some do seem to be less thought out than others. Plus I tend to post update files so that when I do change mine it's easy to print off the changed cards.</p>",
