      "raw": "And if you haven&#39;t checked out my templates you probably should, especially if you have Adobe Illustrator. A great way to make the cards look official or to make them still fit in while playtesting.\n\n<a href=\"http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/forum/topic/custom-card-templates\">http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/forum/topic/custom-card-templates</a>\n\n[quote=\"Spiff\"]\n\nCool.&nbsp; There are a bunch of fan-made heroes and villains on the SotM Boardgame Geek page too, if you&#39;re looking for something new.&nbsp; Seems like most of them get posted before playtesting rather than after, though, so your mileage may vary.\n\n[/quote]\n\nIt&#39;s kind of the point to post them before or during early playtesting, to get feedback on them so they can get balanced out, I know it helped my first hero a lot, but some do seem to be less thought out than others. Plus I tend to post update files so that when I do change mine it&#39;s easy to print off the changed cards.\n",
